alternatives: A straight 45-degree reconciliation of the 0.85 mm profile-height change requires 0.85 mm additional axial run, leaving 2.25 mm to anchor 7.25; the current 3.10 mm stack has only 0.10 mm beyond its 3 mm minimum. Extending the complete body-height cavity loses the quantified root. Enlarging the loading aperture through the full ear width spends the ear bearing at depth 3.00. Moving inserts deeper changes the 8 mm screw stack and loading-tool access.
