alternatives: Filling or sloping down reduces the specified strap opening. A full 45-degree upward roof across its 9 mm fore-aft depth consumes 9 mm of the 3 mm end stock; a two-sided roof needs a 4.5 mm central rise. Moving the strap band changes contact from the fixed collar to the adjacent operating sleeve or tube. A different roof and bearing profile must retain the fixed-collar band, full nominal stock and conditional loop route.
