[thin] Required SB443-IN groove-capture interface: the rail projects 0.700 mm into the 6.650 mm slot and is 0.600 mm along Y. The supplier full-tolerance common groove is only 0.8382 mm wide (1.8542–2.6924 behind the bare pole); the rail occupies 2.000–2.600 mm, and its tips leave 0.1104 mm against the largest groove neck. Mechanically keyed DP420 bedding fills the actual axial groove allowance. magnet-geometry.json binds complete supplier loading, bare-face position and positive keyed capture in this actual exported host. Printed rail/key strength and repeated removal remain unqualified.
alternatives: A 3 mm rail cannot enter this purchased groove. Extending it along Y consumes the recorded supplier groove clearance; increasing its X projection consumes the worst-neck air. Removing it leaves adhesion as the axial restraint. A different magnet or separate bolted retainer changes the purchased interface or adds factory parts and operations.
