[thin] Strict-threshold and rounded-anchor diagnosis at nominal 3 mm construction. Every listed finding prints as 3.000 mm. Exact intersections with the current native solid, extended 0.02 mm beyond both rounded picks, contain a continuous material chord of at least 3.000000 mm through each reported location. The measured bounded chords span 3.000000–3.020000 mm; the upper value can be limited by the chosen extension. The STL ranking at the strict 3 mm boundary does not establish a sub-3 mm native section here. These local measurements do not qualify strength, deposition or lifetime.
alternatives: Correct the reader’s numerical/tessellation boundary using exact native sections when answering this question. Enlarging every nominal section to change floating-point ranking would alter fitted collar, guard and wall interfaces. The lint threshold itself is unchanged.
